               523 class QDP(basic.Basic):                                      
               524     """Quick and Dandy Plot table.                           
               525                                                              
               526     Example::                                                
               527                                                              
               528         ! Initial comment line 1                             
               529         ! Initial comment line 2                             
               530         READ TERR 1                                          
               531         READ SERR 3                                          
               532         ! Table 0 comment                                    
               533         !a a(pos) a(neg) b be c d                            
               534         53000.5   0.25  -0.5   1  1.5  3.5 2                 
               535         54000.5   1.25  -1.5   2  2.5  4.5 3                 
               536         NO NO NO NO NO                                       
               537         ! Table 1 comment                                    
               538         !a a(pos) a(neg) b be c d                            
               539         54000.5   2.25  -2.5   NO  3.5  5.5 5                
               540         55000.5   3.25  -3.5   4  4.5  6.5 nan               
               541                                                              
               542     The input table above contains some initial comments, the
            error commands,                                                     
               543     then two tables.                                         
               544     This file format can contain multiple tables, separated  
            by a line full                                                      
               545     of ``NO``s. Comments are exclamation marks, and missing  
            values are single                                                   
               546     ``NO`` entries. The delimiter is usually whitespace, more
            rarely a comma.                                                     
               547     The QDP format differentiates between data and error     
            columns. The table                                                  
               548     above has commands::                                     
               549                                                              
               550         READ TERR 1                                          
               551         READ SERR 3                                          
               552                                                              
               553     which mean that after data column 1 there will be two    
            error columns                                                       
               554     containing its positive and engative error bars, then    
            data column 2 without                                               
               555     error bars, then column 3, then a column with the        
            symmetric error of column                                           
               556     3, then the remaining data columns.                      
               557                                                              
               558     As explained below, table headers are highly             
            inconsistent. Possible                                              
               559     comments containing column names will be ignored and     
            columns will be called                                              
               560     ``col1``, ``col2``, etc. unless the user specifies their 
            names with the                                                      
               561     ``names=`` keyword argument,                             
               562     When passing column names, pass **only the names of the  
            data columns, not                                                   
               563     the error columns.**                                     
               564     Error information will be encoded in the names of the    
            table columns.                                                      
               565     (e.g. ``a_perr`` and ``a_nerr`` for the positive and     
            negative error of                                                   
               566     column ``a``, ``b_err`` the symmetric error of column    
            ``b``.)                                                             
               567                                                              
               568     When writing tables to this format, users can pass an    
            ``err_specs`` keyword                                               
               569     passing a dictionary ``{'serr': [3], 'terr': [1, 2]}``,  
            meaning that data                                                   
               570     columns 1 and two will have two additional columns each  
            with their positive                                                 
               571     and negative errors, and data column 3 will have an      
            additional column with                                              
               572     a symmetric error (just like the ``READ SERR`` and ``READ
            TERR`` commands                                                     
               573     above)                                                   
               574                                                              
               575     Headers are just comments, and tables distributed by     
            various missions                                                    
               576     can differ greatly in their use of conventions. For      
            example, light curves                                               
               577     distributed by the Swift-Gehrels mission have an extra   
            space in one header                                                 
               578     entry that makes the number of labels inconsistent with  
            the number of cols.                                                 
               579     For this reason, we ignore the comments that might encode
            the column names                                                    
               580     and leave the name specification to the user.            
               581                                                              
               582     Example::                                                
               583                                                              
               584         >               Extra space                          
               585         >                   |                                
               586         >                   v                                
               587         >!     MJD       Err (pos)       Err(neg)        Rate
            Error                                                               
               588         >53000.123456   2.378e-05     -2.378472e-05     NO   
            0.212439                                                            
               589                                                              
               590     These readers and writer classes will strive to          
            understand which of the                                             
               591     comments belong to all the tables, and which ones to each
            single table.                                                       
               592     General comments will be stored in the                   
            ``initial_comments`` meta of each                                   
               593     table. The comments of each table will be stored in the  
            ``comments`` meta.                                                  
               594                                                              
               595     Example::                                                
               596                                                              
               597         t = Table.read(example_qdp, format='ascii.qdp',      
            table_id=1, names=['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'])                             
               598                                                              
               599     reads the second table (``table_id=1``) in file          
